Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Talk Show\"?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0149-1379b394a9a8:d00", "start": 0, "end": 145, "text": "Talk Show (Shae Jones album) Talk Show is the first and only album by R&B singer Shae Jones, released on January 26, 1999 through Uptown Records."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0149-1379b394a9a8:d00", "start": 146, "end": 326, "text": "The album featured heavy input from Jones' mentor Montell Jordan, who served as an executive producer, producer, song writer, arranger and provided background vocals for the album."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0149-1379b394a9a8:d00", "start": 327, "end": 361, "text": "The lead single, \"Talk Show Shhh!\""}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0149-1379b394a9a8:d00", "start": 362, "end": 436, "text": "became a minor hit on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100, peaking at 88 on the chart."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0149-1379b394a9a8:d00", "start": 437, "end": 584, "text": "The album itself, however, was not a commercial success, not selling enough copies to make it to the \"Billboard\" 200 and only found mild success on"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0149-1379b394a9a8:d01", "start": 0, "end": 644, "text": "Bittersweet Druggy Energetic Happy Hypnotic Romantic Sad Sentimental Sexy Trippy All Moods Background Music Celebration Cool & Cocky Drinking Hanging Out In Love Rainy Day Relaxation Road Trip Romantic Evening Sex All Themes Articles My Profile Staff Picks Year in Review Advanced Search Remove Ads New Releases Discover Articles Recommendations My Profile Staff Picks Year In Review Advanced Search Remove Ads 1,000+ album search results for Talk Show Filter By All Result Types Artists Albums Songs Compositions Labels Articles Album Talk Show The Go-Go 's 1984 Pop/Rock Album Talk Show Talk Show 1997 Pop/Rock Album Talk Show Shae Jones 1999"}, "D3S1":